From 6ad277b11e376887f58692e0e25a501c0f8019aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Bokovoy <abokovoy@redhat.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Jun 2026 17:19:07 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 55/91] Add Kerberos principal matching rule plugin for 389-ds

Add a new 389-ds matchingRule plugin (ipa-krbprinc-mr) that implements
Kerberos-aware principal comparison. The krbPrincipalMatch matching
rule (OID 2.16.840.1.113730.3.8.29.1) normalizes principal strings
using krb5_parse_name/krb5_unparse_name, which appends the default
realm when absent, then compares case-insensitively.

This allows the attribute uniqueness plugin to correctly detect that
"user" and "user@REALM" refer to the same principal.

The plugin registers EQUALITY matching callbacks (filter_ava,
values2keys, assertion2keys_ava, compare, normalize) and uses the
default realm from krb5.conf via krb5_get_default_realm().

Fixes: CVE-2026-13097
Signed-off-by: Alexander Bokovoy <abokovoy@redhat.com>
